From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc64 detect Int32 mul/neg overflow in CR0, not XER

ppc64le-v8-int32-overflow-cmpd.patch moved kPPC_Add32 and kPPC_Sub32 off the
XER path.  This does the same for the two remaining Int32 opcodes that still
read XER[OV32] through mcrxrx (ISA 3.0; on POWER8 the emulated mcrxr, or the
loadpc synthesis).

kPPC_Mul32 currently emits

    mullwo rT,rA,rB      SetOE
    mcrxrx cr0           XER[OV32] -> CR0
    extsw  rT,rT         Word32 canonical form
    bc deopt             on CR_OV32

mullw reads only the low word of each operand and writes the *whole* 64-bit
product to RT (Power ISA, Book I, "Multiply Low Word": "The 32-bit operands
are the low-order 32 bits of RA and of RB.  The 64-bit product of the
operands is placed into register RT").  So the int32 result overflows exactly
when the product is not its own sign extension:

    mullw rtmp,rA,rB     LeaveOE
    extsw rT,rtmp        the extsw the canonical form needed anyway
    cmpd  rT,rtmp
    bne   deopt

Three instructions plus the branch on both pools, no XER read, no mulhw.
Unlike the add/sub identity this one does not need the inputs' upper words
to be clean, because mullw never looks at them.  That matters here:
kPPC_LoadWordU32 is lwz, so a negative int32 loaded from memory sits
zero-extended in its register.

kPPC_Neg32 currently emits

    nego   rT,rA         SetOE
    mcrxrx cr0
    extsw  rT,rT
    bc deopt

Int32 negation overflows for exactly one input, INT32_MIN, so the test is a
compare of the input's low word against 0x80000000 and needs no arithmetic
flag at all:

    xoris  rtmp,rA,0x8000   flip bit 31 of the low word
    neg    rT,rA
    extsw  rT,rT
    cmpwi  rtmp,0           CR0[EQ] iff the low word of rA was 0x80000000
    beq    deopt

The 64-bit form neg+extsw+cmpd was considered and rejected: for a
zero-extended INT32_MIN (0x0000000080000000, which is what lwz produces) neg
yields 0xffffffff80000000, which is its own sign extension, and the overflow
is missed; for any other zero-extended negative it reports an overflow that
did not happen.  xoris and cmpwi look only at the low word, so this form is
exact whatever the upper word holds.  The test chain (xoris -> cmpwi) is
independent of the value chain (neg -> extsw), so the branch resolves after
two dependent instructions, the same depth as nego -> mcrxrx.

FlagsConditionToCondition maps kOverflow/kNotOverflow to ne/eq for
kPPC_Mul32, the same polarity as Add32/Sub32, and to eq/ne for kPPC_Neg32,
where CR0 holds a compare against the one overflowing value.  No opcode
produces overflow32/nooverflow32 any more; the cases that consume them are
left in place.

ip holds the untruncated product and the flipped input: it is outside the
allocatable set (r3-r10, r14-r24, r30) and already serves as scratch in this
file.  Both sequences read every input before writing the output, so they
are correct when the output register aliases an input.

Verified on POWER9 (AC922) with a probe that executes the emitted mnemonics:
mullw(0x7fffffff,2) = 0x00000000fffffffe and mullw(0xffffffff00000002,3) =
6, i.e. the full product with the upper words ignored; the mul identity
agreed with mullwo's OV32 and with __builtin_mul_overflow on 196 operand
pairs including garbage upper words; the xoris/cmpwi test agreed with nego's
OV32 on every edge value tried, while neg+extsw+cmpd disagreed on four.

Cost.  POWER9: Mul32 stays at 3 instructions plus the branch, with the
mcrxrx (an XER read serialised behind the multiply) replaced by a cmpd;
Neg32 goes from 3 to 4 plus the branch at the same branch depth.  POWER8:
Mul32 goes from 5 plus the branch (mulhw, mullw, srawi, cmpw, extsw, from
ppc64le-v8-mul32-overflow-synth.patch) to 3; Neg32 from the loadpc
synthesis (neg, and, srwi, mtcrf, mr, extsw -- 6) to 4, and no longer
writes CR through mtcrf.  Neg32 is rare (a checked 0 - x); it is converted
so that no Int32 overflow check in this backend reads XER any more.  No
benchmark was run for this change; the figures are instruction counts.

Valid for both pools: every instruction here is ISA 2.07 or older and
nothing is ISA 3.1.  On the POWER8 pool this supersedes the kPPC_Mul32 hunk
of ppc64le-v8-mul32-overflow-synth.patch and the kPPC_Mul32 lines of its two
FlagsConditionToCondition hunks; that patch's kPPC_Mul64 hunk (mulhd, mulld,
sradi, cmp, with Mul64 -> ne/eq) and its maglev-ir-ppc.cc hunk are not
covered here.  The 64-bit opcodes are untouched -- extsw does not help
there.  Upstreamable as-is; not ppc64le packaging specific.

